<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The HLS player's PlayerView.

    The control bar it names is SHARED with the anime player; see
    player_controls.xml. What stays per player is this file, because the two
    differ in what they ask of the surface itself, not in the bar.

    WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST. app:controller_layout_id is read ONLY from an
    AttributeSet, inside PlayerControlView's playbackAttrs branch, and PlayerView
    forwards its own attrs as playbackAttrs. A PlayerView built in code, which is
    what this replaces, passes null there, so a custom control bar can never
    reach it: media3 silently inflates its stock bar instead, with no error and
    nothing in logcat. Inflating from XML is the only channel, and
    miruro_player_view.xml already proves the pattern in this app.

    EVERY ATTRIBUTE IS STATED, NOT INHERITED. The code this replaces used the
    one argument constructor and took media3's defaults; an XML file that
    quietly differs from them would change behaviour with no code change.

    auto_show stays TRUE because it is the resting value the subtitle UI
    restores to: claimRemoteForSubtitleUi turns auto show off while a panel is
    up and closeAllSubtitleUi turns it back on unconditionally. Setting false
    here would be undone the first time a panel closed.

    The PLAYER layout is deliberately NOT replaced. media3's own carries
    exo_controller_placeholder, without which PlayerView.controller is null and
    around twenty setters throw through checkNotNull, with
    applyControllerPolicy's setControllerShowTimeoutMs the first to hit it. It
    also carries exo_buffering, which is what setShowBuffering draws.
-->
<androidx.media3.ui.PlayerView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    android:id="@+id/hls_player_view"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="@android:color/black"
    app:use_controller="true"
    app:resize_mode="fit"
    app:surface_type="surface_view"
    app:auto_show="true"
    app:keep_content_on_player_reset="false"
    app:controller_layout_id="@layout/player_controls" />
